sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/darwin1859-ch13-18> delphi:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-18--grok> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-18--grok> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 on darwin1859-ch13-18: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.53" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0" ;
    delphi:hasScore "0.533"^^xsd:double ;
    delphi:hasVerdict "partially-resolvable" ;
    delphi:hasConfidence "0.58"^^xsd:double ;
    dct:description "The age contrast in proportions is directly measurable and would clearly confirm or refute the claim for these three domesticated species. The obstacle is data organization: published growth series would have to be compiled study by study, and they cover some dog and horse breeds far better than a balanced sample of pigeon breeds. That is a restricted, paper-by-paper test rather than an analysis of an existing public dataset." ;
    rdfs:comment "Proposed test with existing data: For dog, horse and pigeon breeds, compare multivariate distances among breeds at neonatal or juvenile stages and at adulthood on the same landmarks, excluding or separately noting early-appearing exceptions such as the short-faced tumbler. The claim is confirmed if among-breed distance increases with age for the breed-diagnostic proportions, and refuted if neonates already differ as much as adults across those breeds." ;
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-grok-4.7-high-fast> ;
    delphi:evidenceAgainst "Age-by-breed measurements exist as scattered veterinary and pigeon studies, not as one open morphometric table.", "Breed standards and show data describe adults, so the juvenile half has to be recovered from separate growth papers.", "Body size and allometry change proportions within a breed as it grows, and must be separated from true among-breed divergence." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/darwin1859-ch13-18--grok--operationalizability> a delphi:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Operationalizability of darwin1859-ch13-18 by Grok 4.7: 0.85" ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0-operationalizability> ;
    delphi:assessmentType "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0/operationalizability" ;
